                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6c078fc5-805d-3a0b-bc16-f939d2eac09d",
                        "entry_id": "10c85b52-54d4-3993-b954-f8303c73e2e2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een balspel waarbij een kleine, harde bal met een golfclub van de tee (afslagplaats) weggeslagen wordt in de richting van een met een vlag gemarkeerd punt (de hole)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c16af40e-48c7-4e1d-830b-eacf433d4d6b",
                                "sense_id": "6c078fc5-805d-3a0b-bc16-f939d2eac09d",
                                "text": "Gisteren zette Thomas Pieters zijn eerste officiële stappen op de heilige grond van Augusta National Golf Club in het Amerikaanse Augusta. Net zoals in de Ryder Cup van afgelopen september sloeg hij het publiek met verstomming met subliem golfspel gedurende de eerste 10 holes. Vooraf al kreeg de 25-jarige Antwerpenaar de stempel van ‘in de gaten te houden’ op het hoofd gekleefd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4281c57-cd18-467c-88ea-1d60d5ac3c15",
                                "sense_id": "6c078fc5-805d-3a0b-bc16-f939d2eac09d",
                                "text": ",,Ik ben er trots op dat ik als eerste speler onderdeel uitmaak van deze wereldprimeur op de Europese Tour, vertelde Luiten. ,,Een 360 graden camera loopt met mij mee tijdens de flight en brengt in beeld wat ik zie. Van medespelers tot publiek, van de eerste slag tot de laatste putt. Dichterbij het golfspel kun je als publiek niet komen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4571f4bb-97d5-4731-8b26-f9003a1e2bf6",
                        "source_entry_id": "10c85b52-54d4-3993-b954-f8303c73e2e2",
                        "source_sense_id": "6c078fc5-805d-3a0b-bc16-f939d2eac09d",
                        "target_lang_word": "golf",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "golf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e62afca6-ed78-3665-b3b8-4386f264a920",
                                        "entry_id": "797ff7c5-8f7f-3f05-a41f-2747a09795d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ball game played by individuals competing against one another in which the object is to hit a ball into each of a series of (usually 18 or nine) holes in the minimum number of strokes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c86f4ba0-492d-42f3-9143-b549937c0310",
                                                "sense_id": "e62afca6-ed78-3665-b3b8-4386f264a920",
                                                "text": "In January, China’s state planner said it had ordered the closure of more than 100 golf courses in a multi-year campaign launched in 2011 to tackle illegal development in the sector.\nGolf has also been added to a list of Communist Party disciplinary violations, and is often cited in cases of graft."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed92dd61-0698-3210-b57a-a9dab4db40e2",
                                        "entry_id": "797ff7c5-8f7f-3f05-a41f-2747a09795d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Golf from the NATO/ICAO Phonetic Alphabet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "golf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c94d4711-f864-3d4c-92f3-62ad431f4534",
                                        "entry_id": "fcfe398d-f541-319d-9a95-1d1d752b47d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play the game of golf."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b3707fd-eab0-473a-a383-fd5a90e9b7dd",
                                                "sense_id": "c94d4711-f864-3d4c-92f3-62ad431f4534",
                                                "text": "Last mystery of all, he learned to golf."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e61a2e4c-e97f-32d5-bfe0-53441da8973d",
                                        "entry_id": "fcfe398d-f541-319d-9a95-1d1d752b47d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To write something in as few characters as possible (e.g. in code golf, regex golf)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0329aef6-20c9-4535-8599-7e150f92a685",
                        "source_entry_id": "10c85b52-54d4-3993-b954-f8303c73e2e2",
                        "source_sense_id": "6c078fc5-805d-3a0b-bc16-f939d2eac09d",
                        "target_lang_word": "gulf",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gulf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3433019-3073-391e-9fc5-58542142ec8a",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hollow place in the earth; an abyss; a deep chasm or basin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf9bccb3-97bb-4b08-95ea-c3fc078f273a",
                                                "sense_id": "d3433019-3073-391e-9fc5-58542142ec8a",
                                                "text": "He then surveyed / Hell and the gulf between."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfecaa85-c539-4b3b-b0f1-3434f49492fd",
                                                "sense_id": "d3433019-3073-391e-9fc5-58542142ec8a",
                                                "text": "Of course, there was no arguing against this, but one thing was clear, we could not attempt that leap in the dark; the only thing to do was to wait for the ray of light which pierced through the gulf at sunset."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34339313-d5e7-452e-bbef-c47a7abafa08",
                                                "sense_id": "d3433019-3073-391e-9fc5-58542142ec8a",
                                                "text": "⁠For though my nature rarely yields\n⁠To that vague fear implied in death;\n⁠Nor shudders at the gulfs beneath,\nThe howlings from forgotten fields; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "911f8bf5-13c6-423f-a79f-eab85f25ecd8",
                                                "sense_id": "d3433019-3073-391e-9fc5-58542142ec8a",
                                                "text": "It is told that that traveller came at last to the utter End and there was a mighty gulf, and in the darkness at the bottom of the gulf one small god crept, no bigger than a hare, whose voice came crying in the cold: “I know not.” And beyond the gulf was nought, only the small god crying."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a255dafc-c3d0-373b-9b9c-366d00513215",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which swallows; the gullet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "200a1f8d-dec9-4a63-9238-3ef229f3fb1a",
                                                "sense_id": "a255dafc-c3d0-373b-9b9c-366d00513215",
                                                "text": "Witch's mummy, maw and gulf / Of the ravined salt sea shark,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2e97e3c-a8fa-387b-a108-eaa7991f0af7",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which swallows irretrievably; a whirlpool; a sucking eddy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3473867c-beda-4e21-9130-952d6854281d",
                                                "sense_id": "d2e97e3c-a8fa-387b-a108-eaa7991f0af7",
                                                "text": "[T]here is no such mine, / None; but a gulf of ruin, swallowing gold, not making."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b9cfffe-c0b4-3d49-a5bf-5cc42f503476",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A portion of an ocean or sea extending into the land; a partially landlocked sea"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e308f195-cb86-4245-800f-8747bb81834f",
                                                "sense_id": "8b9cfffe-c0b4-3d49-a5bf-5cc42f503476",
                                                "text": "the Gulf of Mexico"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33a78976-9e87-4138-bcde-5b020033ac55",
                                                "sense_id": "8b9cfffe-c0b4-3d49-a5bf-5cc42f503476",
                                                "text": "the Persian Gulf"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5c5ef15-5b36-3a72-91e9-5bd234010ba2",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large deposit of ore in a lode."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92fe3b51-2325-33a5-b414-74e71c47674b",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wide interval or gap; a separating space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21774a16-fd19-43c3-a450-fd0c9310e6a0",
                                                "sense_id": "92fe3b51-2325-33a5-b414-74e71c47674b",
                                                "text": "Between us and you there is a great gulf fixed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "732e205e-ce1d-4029-b906-a10f7ac7b483",
                                                "sense_id": "92fe3b51-2325-33a5-b414-74e71c47674b",
                                                "text": "`Behold now, let the Dead and Living meet! Across the gulf of Time they still are one.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebd37b58-95d9-3ef1-95e9-2ef8af61d314",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A difference, especially a large difference, between groups."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bdfbe7a-751d-4c2a-a265-5e6f0eaf2ca1",
                                                "sense_id": "ebd37b58-95d9-3ef1-95e9-2ef8af61d314",
                                                "text": "England were graphically illustrating the huge gulf in class between the sides and it was no surprise when Lampard added the second just before the half hour. Steven Gerrard found his Liverpool team-mate Glen Johnson and Lampard arrived in the area with perfect timing to glide a header beyond Namasco."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8eb75bc9-d717-4230-920f-a2e4e87011cc",
                                                "sense_id": "ebd37b58-95d9-3ef1-95e9-2ef8af61d314",
                                                "text": "Piecing together Corbynomics is difficult, not least because it has evolved during Mr Corbyn’s time in charge of Labour. The gulf between the Labour leadership’s past positions and the milder proposals in the manifesto means that enormous uncertainty hangs over what a Corbyn-led government would do in office."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "896d6e3b-7e77-42c0-9e66-7dd03f729e0a",
                                                "sense_id": "ebd37b58-95d9-3ef1-95e9-2ef8af61d314",
                                                "text": "Rich countries must sign a “historic pact” with the poor on the climate, or “we will be doomed”, the UN secretary-general, António Guterres, has warned, as a deepening gulf between the developed and developing world has put climate talks on the brink."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa466720-ea9e-4075-b7d0-3fafaccf250c",
                                                "sense_id": "ebd37b58-95d9-3ef1-95e9-2ef8af61d314",
                                                "text": "The result is a widening gulf between people’s reality and what they are relentlessly told they actually believe in and care about."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce64f772-4654-363c-b0ad-d1637bc10328",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb53b40-eda0-37b7-bd3a-b3bd02bcc0bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The bottom part of a list of those awarded a degree, for those who have only just passed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62247028-cff1-46bc-9092-7441f7f3745e",
                                                "sense_id": "ce64f772-4654-363c-b0ad-d1637bc10328",
                                                "text": "Some ten or fifteen men just on the line, not enough to be plucked or good enough to be placed, are put into the \"gulf,\" as it is popularly called (the Examiners' phrase is \"Degrees allowed\"), and have their degrees given to them but are not printed in the calendar, nor were they at this time allowed to try for the Classical Tripos."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gulf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e15a12b6-9ac8-3e60-bbcb-25a612d69bbc",
                                        "entry_id": "e49fae2f-1e75-3fb4-b4fb-df8724a1decd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To engulf."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44d8d685-0484-46ff-a174-9474f8769b33",
                                                "sense_id": "e15a12b6-9ac8-3e60-bbcb-25a612d69bbc",
                                                "text": "[…] if with thee the roaring wells\n⁠Should gulf him fathom-deep in brine;\n⁠And hands so often clasp’d in mine,\nShould toss with tangle and with shells."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71d5d77c-e0d7-3016-b24b-642d826cf3ee",
                                        "entry_id": "e49fae2f-1e75-3fb4-b4fb-df8724a1decd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To award a degree to somebody who has only just passed sufficiently."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a3095e0-0bde-4db6-9cee-7f19f0a689f9",
                                                "sense_id": "71d5d77c-e0d7-3016-b24b-642d826cf3ee",
                                                "text": "The mention of gulfed and plucked men brings me back to myself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d2f0f7b-8ed0-4baf-b052-9f07cc30e430",
                                                "sense_id": "71d5d77c-e0d7-3016-b24b-642d826cf3ee",
                                                "text": "The good Professor scolded, predicted that they would all be either gulfed or ploughed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f04f42c6-5c46-48d4-aa0a-2d8f7fc8ba79",
                                                "sense_id": "71d5d77c-e0d7-3016-b24b-642d826cf3ee",
                                                "text": "Everyone who knows the Senate House may anticipate the result. When the Tripos of 1822 made its appearance his name did not grace the list. In short, to use the expressive vocabulary of the university, Macaulay was gulfed:—a mishap which disabled him from contending for the Chancellor's medals, then the crowning trophies of a classical career."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
